at helium is less dense than air, and considering how sound waves behave in different mediums, it's reasonable to conclude that the increased speed of sound waves through helium could indeed make voices sound deeper to the listener.", "new_cot_probs": [1.0, 0.0], "cot_prob": [-177.0], "cot_step_prob": [-177.0]}}}
